25lNjU1MDM3","number":6,"title":"backlog","description":"Low priority items. We plan to work on this but don't have a target date.","creator":{"login":"justinmk","id":1359421,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNTk0MjE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1359421?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk","html_url":"https://github.com/justinmk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":640,"closed_issues":761,"state":"open","created_at":"2014-05-10T20:43:04Z","updated_at":"2025-12-12T21:14:43Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":0,"created_at":"2015-08-26T21:19:14Z","updated_at":"2016-02-28T16:49:08Z","closed_at":"2016-02-28T16:49:05Z","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"There is a known (at least, I remember it reported by me and noticed by Bram) bug in string(): if it represents a floating-point value which is either infinite or not a number then it returns `[-]inf` or `[-]nan` (on my system the latter is always `-nan` for some reason), but this output cannot be `eval()`ed back. If there were `v:inf` and `v:nan` variables then it would be possible to represent those values as `[-]v:inf` and `v:nan` respectively and `eval()` the result back. Necessary values are available as `math.h` macros `INFINITE` and `NAN`, latter is optional (it _must_ be present if floating-point implementation supports NaN values, and _must not_ if it does not). Both macros are supposed to have `float` types though, I hope there will be no problems from casting these rather special values to double (which is what (Neo)Vim use for floating-point values).\n","closed_by":{"login":"justinmk","id":1359421,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNTk0MjE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1359421?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk","html_url":"https://github.com/justinmk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/issues/3248/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/issues/3248/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}